GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/codekg/unit/test_visitor_scoping.py> {
    ns6:test_visitor_scoping.py dcterms:identifier "tests.codekg.unit.test_visitor_scoping" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Call-graph scoping and repeated definitions in visitor.extract_module() (GitHub issues #102 and #84).

Python scoping: a class body is not an enclosing scope for its methods, a parameter or local variable hides a module
function of the same name, and a nested function's calls belong to the nested function. One IRI per name, so a property's
setter and an ``@overload`` series must not write conflicting facts about it.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_visitor_scoping" ;
