    ns50:TestNativeBackendVersionConformance dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_conformance.TestNativeBackendVersionConformance" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """StarLayerGraph(backend='rdf-1.2') sends SPARQL straight through to a
real endpoint via HTTP with zero rewriting (correct - Fuseki/Oxigraph
understand VERSION natively), which means query()/update() never call
rewrite_sparql12_to_11 and so never ran this check at all until fixed.

Confirmed live 2026-07-17 against Fuseki 5.5.0 and Oxigraph: both
execute a VERSION "1.2-basic" + <<( )>> query normally (HTTP 200) with
no warning or error signal anywhere in the response - so without this
fix, a native-backend StarLayerGraph would silently never emit
SPARQL12ConformanceWarning for the identical query the default in-memory
backend does warn on, an inconsistency this project otherwise takes
care to avoid (see tests/integration/test_cross_backend_parity.py).

check_native_version_conformance() is pure Python logic with no network
dependency (the network call happens after it, in native_query()/
http_update()), so it's tested directly here rather than requiring a
live backend.""" ;
        rdfs:label "TestNativeBackendVersionConformance" ;
        ns2:declares ns50:TestNativeBackendVersionConformance.test_1_2_basic_with_triple_term_warns, ns50:TestNativeBackendVersionConformance.test_unrecognized_version_label_warns, ns50:TestNativeBackendVersionConformance.test_1_2_basic_without_triple_term_does_not_warn, ns50:TestNativeBackendVersionConformance.test_no_version_directive_does_not_warn ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_conformance.py" ;
        ns2:lineEnd 300 ;
        ns2:lineStart 260 .

    ns50:TestNativeBackendVersionConformance.test_1_2_basic_with_triple_term_warns dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_conformance.TestNativeBackendVersionConformance.test_1_2_basic_with_triple_term_warns" ;
