    ns59:TestDefaultGraphIsAStarLayerGraph.test_default_graph_stays_current_after_turtle12_reroute_parse dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_dataset.TestDefaultGraphIsAStarLayerGraph.test_default_graph_stays_current_after_turtle12_reroute_parse" ;
        a ns2:Method ;
        rdfs:comment """A second, narrower staleness bug than the two above: parse()
routes format='turtle12' (and 'n3'/'n3-12'/'text/n3', which alias to
it) through trig12's parser, which populates the default graph via
_load_context()/_register_sg() - a *new* StarLayerGraph swapped into
_sg_cache, never touching whatever object a one-time-cached
self._default_context pointed at. Before the fix, default_graph
kept returning that stale, registry-empty pre-parse object, so
has_triple_term() here returned False even though the triple parsed
correctly and even round-tripped correctly through serialize()
(which reaches the current object via get_context(), not
default_graph). longturtle12/nt12/rdfxml12/manchester don't hit
this - they parse straight into self.default_graph.parse() instead
of rerouting through trig12 - so this is specific to turtle12/n3.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_default_graph_stays_current_after_turtle12_reroute_parse" ;
        ns2:calls ns59:ex ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_dataset.py" ;
        ns2:lineEnd 499 ;
        ns2:lineStart 478 ;
        ns2:signature "def test_default_graph_stays_current_after_turtle12_reroute_parse(self)" .

    ns59:TestDefaultGraphIsAStarLayerGraph.test_graphs_yields_the_default_graph_as_a_starlayergraph dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_dataset.TestDefaultGraphIsAStarLayerGraph.test_graphs_yields_the_default_graph_as_a_starlayergraph" ;
        a ns2:Method ;
        rdfs:comment """graphs() yields from super(Dataset, self).contexts(), which
returns whatever self._default_context actually is - this is the
same fix as above, verified from the graphs() call site too.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_graphs_yields_the_default_graph_as_a_starlayergraph" ;
        ns2:calls ns59:ex ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_dataset.py" ;
        ns2:lineEnd 476 ;
        ns2:lineStart 469 ;
        ns2:signature "def test_graphs_yields_the_default_graph_as_a_starlayergraph(self)" .

    ns59:TestDefaultUnionPropagation dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_dataset.TestDefaultUnionPropagation" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """default_union=True must be honored consistently across every entry
point, the same way self.triples() honors it (see TestQuads above) -
not just the one that happened to get tested first. .query() and
.update() each build their own internal Dataset/Graph wrapper for
execution (_build_raw_execution_graph() and .update()'s in-memory
branch, respectively) and previously constructed it with the rdflib
default (default_union=False) regardless of self.default_union, so a
GRAPH-less query/update pattern silently saw nothing from any named
graph even when the dataset was explicitly configured to union them.""" ;
        rdfs:label "TestDefaultUnionPropagation" ;
        ns2:declares ns59:TestDefaultUnionPropagation.test_query_graphless_pattern_empty_when_default_union_false, ns59:TestDefaultUnionPropagation.test_update_graphless_where_matches_named_graphs, ns59:TestDefaultUnionPropagation.test_query_graphless_pattern_sees_named_graphs, ns59:TestDefaultUnionPropagation.test_update_graphless_where_empty_when_default_union_false ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_dataset.py" ;
        ns2:lineEnd 385 ;
        ns2:lineStart 331 .

