GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_triple_term_value_equality.py> {
    ns45:test_triple_term_value_equality.py dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_triple_term_value_equality" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """`=` and `IN` between triple terms compare components by value (GitHub issue #74).

SPARQL 1.2 sameValue step 4 compares the components pairwise, so
<<(:s :p 1)>> = <<(:s :p 1.0)>> is true. Triple terms built inside the query
(constants, TRIPLE()) used to compare by name, and IN never used the rule.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_triple_term_value_equality" ;
        ns2:declares ns143:test_bound_triple_terms_compare_by_value_in_filter_and_in, ns143:test_constant_triple_terms_compare_by_value ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_triple_term_value_equality.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:pytest .

