    ns196:test_unique_values_for_via_node_self_reference_terminates_and_still_finds_the_violation dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_native_component_composition.test_unique_values_for_via_node_self_reference_terminates_and_still_finds_the_violation" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """A shape that both declares sh:uniqueValuesFor (triggering the
full-batch path) and references itself via sh:node - genuine shape
recursion reached through the *new* full-batch mechanism, not the
logical operators. It refers back to the very same nodes, so it is a
cycle: it must stop (no hang, no RecursionError) and the cross-node check
itself must still be evaluated correctly. Since GitHub issue #26 the cut
is the exact one in ``starlayer.shacl.recursion`` (the same shape on the
same batch of nodes again is assumed to conform), so no
ShapeRecursionWarning is raised, and the revisit is counted.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_unique_values_for_via_node_self_reference_terminates_and_still_finds_the_violation" ;
        ns2:calls ns196:_validate ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_native_component_composition.py" ;
