GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_select_widgets_per_shape.py> {
    ns163:test_select_widgets_per_shape.py dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_select_widgets_per_shape" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """``select_widgets(per="shape")``: one answer per property shape, finished per node (GitHub issue #14).

A UI shows many nodes of the same shape. ``select_widgets`` used to redo, for every node, the checks that depend only on
the shape. With ``per="shape"`` those are done once; ``choice.resolve(node, data)`` validates only the conditions that read
a node's data. The answer must not change, so each is checked against ``select_widget`` for the same node.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_select_widgets_per_shape" ;
        ns2:declares ns226:test_the_shape_conditions_are_checked_once_however_many_nodes_follow, ns226:_graph, ns226:test_the_schema_method_passes_per_through, ns226:test_a_preference_is_the_first_candidate, ns226:test_with_no_data_condition_one_answer_serves_every_node, ns226:test_the_candidates_stop_at_the_first_one_that_needs_no_data, ns226:test_the_generic_catalog_never_needs_a_node, ns226:test_per_shape_takes_no_node, ns226:test_resolving_gives_the_same_widget_as_choosing_per_node, ns226:shapes, ns226:data ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_select_widgets_per_shape.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:pytest, ns4:rdflib .

