    ns163:test_target_where_isolation.py dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_target_where_isolation" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """sh:targetWhere decides which nodes are targets by validating them against the where-shape ONLY (GitHub issue #53).

The nested validation used to run the whole shapes graph, so a violation of any unrelated shape on a candidate node made that
node look non-conforming to the where-shape, and it silently stopped being a target.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_target_where_isolation" ;
