GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/sqe_coverage/test_parser_differential.py> {
    ns291:test_parser_differential.py dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.sqe_coverage.test_parser_differential" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Differential and consistency testing of the regular query path (``StarLayerGraph``/``StarLayerDataset``
``.query()``: ``parse_query_12``, lowering, execution), using the same generated queries as the sqe
property tests. The sqe tests treat that path as the oracle; these tests hold the oracle itself to account.

* ``test_matches_plain_rdflib``: every generated query is SPARQL 1.1, so plain rdflib is an independent
  reference. Both are run on the same data; the rows (or the kind of run-time error) must agree.
* ``test_prepare_and_reserialize_round_trip``: ``prepare_query_12`` followed by the project's own 1.2
  serializer must give text that returns the same rows as the original.

Opt-in (``pytest --sqe-coverage``); example count from ``STARLAYER_SQE_FUZZ_EXAMPLES``.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_parser_differential" ;
        ns2:declares ns294:test_matches_plain_rdflib, ns294:test_prepare_and_reserialize_round_trip, ns294:_outcome ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/sqe_coverage/test_parser_differential.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:rdflib, ns4:pytest, ns4:tests.sparql.sqe_coverage.test_sqe_features, ns4:tests.sparql.sqe_coverage.test_sqe_property_based, ns4:__future__, ns4:hypothesis .

