GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/unit/test_entailment_rdfs.py> {
    ns300:test_entailment_rdfs.py dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.unit.test_entailment_rdfs" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """tests/unit/test_entailment_rdfs.py

Coverage for starlayer.sparql.entailment_rdfs.rewrite_algebra_for_rdfs - the
query-time RDFS rewrite, independent of StarLayerGraph's own entailment=
wiring (see packages/graph/tests/unit/test_entailment.py for that
end-to-end coverage).

Per this project's own testing discipline (this package's own CLAUDE.md:
"any new query/update shape needs an execution-comparison test, not just a
structural one"), most tests compare rewritten-query results directly
against owlrl.RDFS_Semantics run on the same data - owlrl is the oracle.
Two known, deliberate divergences from raw owlrl output are documented and
tested explicitly rather than papered over (see the module docstring in
entailment_rdfs.py): this rewrite's subClassOf*/subPropertyOf* reflexivity
is unconditional (a superset of owlrl's stricter "only if explicitly typed
rdfs:Class/rdf:Property" reflexivity - rdfs6/rdfs10), and it deliberately
excludes the "vocabulary-level" rules (rdfs4a/4b/8/12/13, the ~30 fixed
axiomatic triples) that account for most of a real RDFS closure's size
without answering any actual question about the data.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_entailment_rdfs" ;
        ns2:declares ns307:_materialize, ns307:TestSubPropertyOf, ns307:TestDomainAndRange, ns307:TestMixedQuery, ns307:_query, ns307:TestSubClassOf, ns307:TestDeliberateExclusions, ns307:TestSubClassOfAsQueryPredicate ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/unit/test_entailment_rdfs.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns4:pytest, ns4:rdflib.plugins.sparql, ns4:owlrl, ns4:rdflib .

    ns307:TestDeliberateExclusions dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.unit.test_entailment_rdfs.TestDeliberateExclusions" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """The rewrite does NOT chase the "vocabulary-level" rules - see
entailment_rdfs.py's module docstring for why. These tests pin that
scope down explicitly, rather than leaving it as an implicit gap a
future change could silently widen or narrow without anyone noticing.""" ;
        rdfs:label "TestDeliberateExclusions" ;
        ns2:declares ns307:TestDeliberateExclusions.test_does_not_entail_universal_rdfs_resource_typing, ns307:TestDeliberateExclusions.test_does_not_entail_rdf_property_typing_for_used_predicates ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/unit/test_entailment_rdfs.py" ;
        ns2:lineEnd 208 ;
        ns2:lineStart 191 .

