GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/starontology/manchester_conformance/tools/mutation_scan.py> {
    ns368:mutation_scan.py dcterms:identifier "tests.starontology.manchester_conformance.tools.mutation_scan" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Mutation scan of manchester_shapes.ttl: how well do the shapes tell a broken tree from a good one?

Takes the tree of every corpus case, and applies each mutation operator once per distinct
(node class, property, operator) it finds. For every mutant it records whether the shapes REJECT it,
whether it VALIDATES and still decodes (usually a legitimate optional thing removed), or - the finding
that matters - whether it passes validation yet CRASHES the decoder: a hole in the shapes.

    python tests/starontology/manchester_conformance/tools/mutation_scan.py [--out mutants.json]

About 430 mutants, ~4 minutes (each is a SHACL run). Not part of the test run; the fast regression
version is test_mc_shapes_mutation.py.

Operators: remove a triple; replace a value by a literal; add a second value; drop an rdf:type; break an
rdf:List's termination.""" ;
        rdfs:label "mutation_scan" ;
        ns2:declares ns369:local, ns369:verdict, ns369:types_of, ns369:main ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/starontology/manchester_conformance/tools/mutation_scan.py" ;
